<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lê Trang Tông</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1515–1548</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Le Trang Tong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lê Trang Tông was emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> from 1533 to 1548, the first ruler of the restored Later Lê line. Enthroned in exile by the loyalist general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguyen-kim">Nguyễn Kim</a>, who opposed the Mạc dynasty, he reigned in the hills of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laos">Laos</a> and Thanh Hóa while real power passed to Nguyễn Kim and later to the Trịnh lords.</p></div>
